UIOP/ASDF porting: implementation-specific API UIOP expects, to be provided as BOCL
extensions (+ #+bocl clauses in UIOP's dispatch points).

STATUS: open (analysis).  ASDF ships UIOP, a portability layer that dispatches per
implementation (#+sbcl/#+ccl/... and falls back to NOT-IMPLEMENTED-ERROR for unknown
Lisps).  bocl already exports :BOCL in *FEATURES*, so the port is: implement the
primitives below in BOCL, then add #+bocl branches to the UIOP files cited.
References are to modules/asdf-src/uiop/.

== Already present in bocl ==
machine-instance, compile-file, truename, probe-file, merge-pathnames, BOCL:QUIT,
*FEATURES* has :BOCL :64-BIT-*.   Missing/!weak noted below.

== TIER 1 — UIOP will not initialise without these ==

1. *FEATURES* — add OS/arch keywords UIOP keys on: :UNIX (and :LINUX / :DARWIN),
   :X86-64 / :ARM64.  UIOP derives os-unix/os-windows and arch from these
   (uiop/os.lisp detect-os, *features*).  bocl has :BOCL but no :UNIX today.

2. os.lisp — environment + cwd (each is a per-impl one-liner + NOT-IMPLEMENTED-ERROR):
   - GETENV name -> string|nil                        (os.lisp:120)  => bocl:getenv
   - (SETF GETENV) / SETENV, UNSETENV                 (os.lisp:137,149)
   - GETCWD -> pathname                               (os.lisp:342)  => bocl:getcwd
   - CHDIR path                                       (os.lisp:361)  => bocl:chdir

3. image.lisp — process:
   - QUIT code (have BOCL:QUIT; add #+bocl (bocl:quit code))   (image.lisp:82)
   - RAW-COMMAND-LINE-ARGUMENTS -> list of strings    (image.lisp:241)
       => bocl:*command-line-arguments* / bocl:command-line-arguments (the raw argv)

4. filesystem.lisp / pathname.lisp — CL:DIRECTORY must enumerate a wildcard
   ("dir/*.*", "dir/**/*.lisp"); bocl's DIRECTORY currently returns NIL for wildcards.
   The kernel now has %LIST-DIRECTORY (sources/bocl.c) to build on.  UIOP also wants
   NATIVE-NAMESTRING / PARSE-NATIVE-NAMESTRING and ENSURE-DIRECTORIES-EXIST,
   DELETE-FILE-IF-EXISTS, RENAME-FILE-OVERWRITING-TARGET, FILE-WRITE-DATE (mostly
   standard; verify wild-pathname + logical-pathname coverage — bocl pathnames are
   partial, doc §19).

5. Conditions — UIOP/ASDF WARN STYLE-WARNING subclasses; bocl's CLOS condition
   hierarchy is broken (see issue clos-condition-hierarchy-parents).  Fix that so
   (typep x 'warning) etc. hold; this is the first error hit loading ASDF.

== TIER 2 — needed by RUN-PROGRAM and the compile path ==

6. run-program.lisp — a subprocess facility.  Minimum: a synchronous %SYSTEM(command)
   that runs a shell command and returns its exit code (run-program.lisp:462, the
   %use-system fallback) => bocl:run-program / bocl:%system (fork+exec+waitpid, or
   posix system(3)).  ASDF core does not need it, but many systems' build ops do.

7. lisp-build.lisp — COMPILE-FILE* wraps CL:COMPILE-FILE and must capture conditions:
   CL:COMPILE-FILE returning (values output-truename warnings-p failure-p), plus
   HANDLER-BIND on WARNING/STYLE-WARNING/ERROR so UIOP can classify
   compile-warned-error / compile-failed-error (lisp-build.lisp:207-244).  bocl has
   COMPILE-FILE (minimal compilation) + *DEFAULT-COMPILED-FILE-TYPE* "fasl"; verify
   the multiple-value return and condition signalling.

== TIER 3 — optional / degradable (UIOP tolerates NOT-IMPLEMENTED-ERROR) ==

8. launch-program.lisp — full async spawn: LAUNCH-PROGRAM with stdin/stdout/stderr
   redirection, PROCESS-INFO-PID, %PROCESS-STATUS, WAIT-PROCESS, TERMINATE-PROCESS
   (launch-program.lisp:546,269,287,365,466).  Needs real pipe/fork/exec/waitpid.
9. image.lisp DUMP-IMAGE / CREATE-IMAGE (save an executable)        (image.lisp:361,431).
10. lisp-build.lisp COMBINE-FASLS (monolithic bundles)              (lisp-build.lisp:846),
    and the SBCL-only deferred-warnings machinery (return nil is fine).

== Suggested approach ==
- Implement Tier-1 BOCL primitives (getenv/setenv/getcwd/chdir, command-line-args,
  working wildcard DIRECTORY) and add :UNIX etc. to *FEATURES*; fix the condition
  hierarchy.  That should get UIOP/ASDF to load and define systems.
- Add a small #+bocl porting patch to the UIOP files above (kept as a bocl-side patch
  or upstreamed) so each dispatch calls the bocl primitive.
- Add bocl:run-program (%system) for Tier 2; defer Tier 3.
- Re-run the must-* suite after each step (esp. must-condition for the hierarchy fix).

----------------------------------------------------------------------
PROGRESS (slice 125, v1.3.12) — TIER 1 DONE
----------------------------------------------------------------------
DONE:
- *FEATURES* += :UNIX :LINUX/:DARWIN :X86-64/:ARM64 (kernel.c).
- Kernel %GETENV/%SETENV/%UNSETENV, %GETCWD, %CHDIR, %COMMAND-LINE-ARGUMENTS,
  %DIRECTORY-P (bocl.c); BOCL wrappers bocl:getenv/setenv/unsetenv/getcwd/chdir/
  command-line-arguments (+ *command-line-arguments*).
- CL:DIRECTORY: real glob (*, ?, ** wild-inferiors) over %LIST-DIRECTORY/%DIRECTORY-P.
- CLOS condition hierarchy fixed (see clos-condition-hierarchy-parents): style-warning
  is now TYPEP 'warning, etc.
No regressions (must-condition 147/0, -sequence 3851/0, -cons 728/0, -symbol 113/0).

ASDF LOAD PROGRESS (loading modules/asdf/asdf.lisp directly):
- The FIRST error (WARN of a STYLE-WARNING subclass) is GONE — UIOP's
  DEFINE-PACKAGE-STYLE-WARNING now just warns, as it should.
- NEXT blocker: SIMPLE-TYPE-ERROR "The value NIL is not of type PACKAGE", raised in
  UIOP's DEFINE-PACKAGE (uiop/package.lisp) package surgery — some package op returns
  / is handed NIL where a package object is expected (e.g. find-package of a not-yet-
  existing package used as an argument, or rename/use of NIL).  This begins the
  iterative ASDF-compat work; it is NOT a Tier-1 item.
  Note: UIOP's DEFINE-PACKAGE is a large reimplementation of DEFPACKAGE with package
  recycling and conflict resolution — it exercises far more of the package API than
  CL:DEFPACKAGE; expect several package-system gaps here.

REMAINING toward a loadable ASDF (separate, iterative):
- A #+bocl UIOP port: redefine the still-NOT-IMPLEMENTED uiop functions to call the
  bocl: primitives (getenv/getcwd/chdir/quit/raw-command-line-arguments).  Currently
  unnecessary for the FIRST stages (UIOP's own definitions error only when CALLED),
  but needed before run-program / image ops are used.
- Work through UIOP's DEFINE-PACKAGE package-API needs, then Tier-2 (run-program,
  compile-file* condition capture).
